IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc5-logic`
IMPORT `ssc5-part7`

-- Tests for ssc5-part7.l4 (Part VII, ss 123 to 137).  Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- section named beside it, before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding, not something to edit away.

§ `Tests -- Part VII`

§§ `s 123 -- income-related benefits and the schemes`

#ASSERT `s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` `income support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` `housing benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` `council tax benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another benefit: the list does not say "only", so NOTHING, not FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` `child benefit` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` `attendance allowance` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): copies at local offices of the DWP, at all reasonable hours, without payment.
#ASSERT `s 123(2) the person may inspect a copy of the scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(2) the person may inspect a copy of the scheme without payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(2) the person may inspect a copy of the scheme without payment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(2) the person may inspect a copy of the scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a), (3)(b), (4)(a), (4)(b)
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the housing benefit scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the housing benefit scheme without payment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the housing benefit scheme without payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(3)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the housing benefit scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the council tax benefit scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the council tax benefit scheme without payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the council tax benefit scheme without payment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 123(4)(b) the person may inspect a copy of the council tax benefit scheme without payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative twins.  A #TRACE prints its outcome and no assertion line, so these are run, and read, not counted:
-- the right party doing the duty fulfils it (FULFILLED); the duty stays open until it is done.
#TRACE `s 123(2) the Secretary of State's duty to make copies of the schemes available` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 123 the Secretary of State` DOES `s 123 make copies of the scheme available for public inspection without payment` AT 3
#TRACE `s 123(3)(a) the housing benefit authority's duty to make persons aware` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 123 an authority granting housing benefit` DOES `s 123 take the steps that appear appropriate to secure that persons who may be entitled become aware that they may be entitled` AT 3
#TRACE `s 123(3)(b) the housing benefit authority's duty to make copies of its scheme available` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 123 an authority granting housing benefit` DOES `s 123 make copies of the scheme available for public inspection without payment` AT 3
#TRACE `s 123(4)(a) the billing authority's duty to make persons aware` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 123 a billing authority or, in Scotland, a local authority` DOES `s 123 take the steps that appear appropriate to secure that persons who may be entitled become aware that they may be entitled` AT 3
#TRACE `s 123(4)(b) the billing authority's duty to make copies of its scheme available` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 123 a billing authority or, in Scotland, a local authority` DOES `s 123 make copies of the scheme available for public inspection without payment` AT 3

§§ `s 124 -- income support`

-- Positional records, in the order of the DECLARE:
--   in GB | at/over QA | no income | income | applicable | engaged | couple | other engaged | within 15 days | rel. education | prescribed edu. circs | prescribed category | JSA | other JSA | IB-JSA couple | other SPC | ESA | other ESA
`s 124(1) test claimant, every condition met` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, not in Great Britain` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, at the qualifying age` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, income equal to the applicable amount` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 100, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, income above the applicable amount` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 100.01, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, no income` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 999, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, working` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, working, in the 15 days after return` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, partner working` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, partner working, in the 15 days after return` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, a flag about a partner but not a couple` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s 124(1) test claimant, in relevant education` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, in relevant education in prescribed circumstances` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, not in a prescribed category` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, couple entitled to an income-based jobseeker's allowance` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to state pension credit` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, entitled to an employment and support allowance` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to an income-related employment and support allowance` MEANS `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 30, 100, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, every condition met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) "of or over the age of 16": the answer of s 173(a) is passed on; a "no" is a no, an unknown stays unknown.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST FALSE) `s 124(1) test claimant, every condition met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` NOTHING `s 124(1) test claimant, every condition met` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` NOTHING `s 124(1) test claimant, not in Great Britain` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, not in Great Britain` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, at the qualifying age` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) "does not exceed the applicable amount": equal passes; a penny over fails; no income passes whatever the figure.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, income equal to the applicable amount` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, income above the applicable amount` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, no income` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) not engaged in remunerative work, nor the other member of a couple.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, working` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, partner working` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Section 127(b): in the 15 days after a return to work, only the other member's work bars.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, working, in the 15 days after return` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, partner working, in the 15 days after return` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A flag about a partner for a person who is not a member of a couple does not count.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, a flag about a partner but not a couple` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) relevant education, except in prescribed circumstances.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, in relevant education` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, in relevant education in prescribed circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) a prescribed category.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, not in a prescribed category` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f) no jobseeker's allowance for the person, the partner, or the couple's income-based allowance.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, couple entitled to an income-based jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (g) the other member of the couple is not entitled to state pension credit.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to state pension credit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (h) no employment and support allowance for the person, nor income-related for the other member.
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, entitled to an employment and support allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` (JUST TRUE) `s 124(1) test claimant, partner entitled to an income-related employment and support allowance` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (1A) with (1B).
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): arguments: entitled; no income; income; applicable amount; period under a week.
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) TRUE 0 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) FALSE 30 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST 70
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) FALSE 100 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) FALSE 130 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) FALSE 30 100 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` (JUST FALSE) FALSE 30 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` NOTHING FALSE 30 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), (6)
#ASSERT `s 124(5) the amount payable for the period in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 42) EQUALS JUST 42
#ASSERT `s 124(5) the amount payable for the period in pounds` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(5) the amount payable for the period in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 42) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` 6 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` 7 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 124(7) the allowance is an income-related employment and support allowance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 124(7) the allowance is an income-related employment and support allowance` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 126, s 127 -- trade disputes and return to work`

-- (2) the maternity period.  10 January 2024 was a Wednesday: its week began Sunday 7 January; the 6th week before
-- began 42 days earlier, Sunday 26 November 2023.  Confinement on Saturday 20 January 2024: its week began Sunday
-- 14 January; the 7th week after ends 55 days later, Saturday 9 March 2024.
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 10 1 2024) (Date 20 1 2024))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 26 11 2023
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 10 1 2024) (Date 20 1 2024))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 9 3 2024
-- The expected date on the Sunday that begins its week, and on the Saturday that ends it: the same week.
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 7 1 2024) (Date 14 1 2024))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 26 11 2023
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 13 1 2024) (Date 14 1 2024))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 26 11 2023
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 14 1 2024) (Date 14 1 2024))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 3 12 2023
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 7 1 2024) (Date 20 1 2024))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 9 3 2024
#ASSERT (`s 126(2) the maternity period` (Date 7 1 2024) (Date 21 1 2024))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 16 3 2024

-- (1): arguments: under 16; prescribed description; (a); (b); incapacity shown; maternity period shown.
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): the nearest lower multiple of 5p.
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` 50.01 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` 50.05 EQUALS 50.05
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` 50.09 EQUALS 50.05
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` 50.10 EQUALS 50.10
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` 0.04 EQUALS 0
-- (3): arguments: the case; the applicable amount; the portion in respect of them; the further portion.
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(a) the person is not a member of a family` 100 40 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(b) the person is a member of a family but not of a couple` 100 40 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(c)(i) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount consists only of an amount in respect of them` 100 100 0 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(c)(i) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount consists only of an amount in respect of them` 100.12 100.12 0 EQUALS 50.05
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(c)(ii) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount includes other amounts` 150 80 10 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(c)(ii) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount includes other amounts` 150 80.14 10 EQUALS 99.91
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(d)(i) the section applies to both members of a couple and neither is responsible for a child or a person of a prescribed description who is a member of the same household` 150 80 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` `s 126(3)(d)(ii) the section applies to both members of a couple in any other case` 150 80 10 EQUALS 60
-- (5)(a): arguments: income apart from the payments; (i) payment; (ii) tax repayment; regulations provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(a) the income taken into account in pounds` 20 15 5.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 40.5
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(a) the income taken into account in pounds` 20 15 5.5 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(b): not made at or below the relevant sum; otherwise the difference.
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` 53 53 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` 52.99 53 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` 53.01 53 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.01
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` 80 53 FALSE EQUALS JUST 27
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` 80 53 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7), (8)
#ASSERT `s 126(7) the relevant sum in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS 53
#ASSERT `s 126(7) the relevant sum in pounds` (JUST 55) EQUALS 55
-- 53 increased by 3.5% is 54.855, remainder 35p over 54.50, which is nearer 55.00 than 54.50.
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 53 3.5 EQUALS 55
-- 50 increased by 8.5% is 54.25: a remainder of exactly 25p is disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 50 8.5 EQUALS 54
-- 54.20: remainder 20p, nearer 54.00.  54.26: remainder 26p, nearer 54.50.  54.30: 30p, nearer 54.50.  55.00: already a multiple.
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 50 8.4 EQUALS 54
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 50 8.52 EQUALS 54.5
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 50 8.6 EQUALS 54.5
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` 50 10 EQUALS 55

-- s 127: the person returned to work on 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `s 127(a) section 126 applies to the person on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 127(a) section 126 applies to the person on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 2 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 127(a) section 126 applies to the person on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(a) section 126 applies to the person on the day` FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 2 3 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The 15 days are 1 March to 15 March 2024 inclusive.
#ASSERT `s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 15 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 16 3 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` TRUE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 5 3 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` TRUE `s 127(c) the person to whom the sum was paid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` TRUE `s 127(c) a prescribed person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` TRUE `s 127(c) a prescribed person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` TRUE `s 127(c) the other member of the couple` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` TRUE `s 127(c) the other member of the couple` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` FALSE `s 127(c) the person to whom the sum was paid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 130 -- housing benefit`

#ASSERT `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds` (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 130A(7) the determination is a rent officer determination` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130A(7) the determination is a rent officer determination` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): prescribed; council tax and mortgage payments cannot be prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 130(2) the payment is a payment in respect of a dwelling` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130(2) the payment is a payment in respect of a dwelling` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 130(2) the payment is a payment in respect of a dwelling` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 130(2) the payment is a payment in respect of a dwelling` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): arguments: liable; AMHB; no income; income; applicable amount; rate of deduction as a fraction.
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE (JUST 100) FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Income above the applicable amount by 200 with a rate of 0.5 takes the whole AMHB of 100: nothing remains.
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE (JUST 100) FALSE 280 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE (JUST 100) FALSE 279.99 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE (JUST 100) TRUE 999 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` FALSE (JUST 100) FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE NOTHING FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` FALSE NOTHING FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` TRUE NOTHING FALSE 100 80 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments: entitled; AMHB; no income; income; applicable amount; rate.
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) FALSE 100 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) TRUE 0 80 0.5 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 100) FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` NOTHING (JUST 100) FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE 80 80 0.5 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 134 to 136A`

-- (1): a capital limit of 16,000 is used only to place the boundary: the amount is the prescribed one.
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the person is barred from the income-related benefit by capital` 16000 0 16000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the person is barred from the income-related benefit by capital` 16000.01 0 16000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the person is barred from the income-related benefit by capital` 5000 16001 16000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(1) the person is barred from the income-related benefit by capital` 5000 6000 16000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the person's entitlement is excluded by another member's entitlement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the person's entitlement is excluded by another member's entitlement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the person's entitlement is excluded by another member's entitlement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 134(2) the person's entitlement is excluded by another member's entitlement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): an amount of 4.99 against a prescribed amount of 5.00.
#ASSERT `s 134(4) the income-related benefit is not payable` 4.99 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134(4) the income-related benefit is not payable` 5 5 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 134(4) the income-related benefit is not payable` 4.99 5 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the applicable amount in pounds` (LIST 10, 20.5) EQUALS 30.5
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the applicable amount in pounds` EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 135(1) the applicable amount in pounds` (LIST 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 135(5) the applicable amount includes an amount for being severely disabled` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 135(5) the applicable amount includes an amount for being severely disabled` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the amount treated as the claimant's in pounds` TRUE (LIST 100, 50) FALSE EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the amount treated as the claimant's in pounds` TRUE (LIST 100, 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 136(1) the amount treated as the claimant's in pounds` FALSE (LIST 100) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 136A(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the benefit and the person` `s 136A(1) housing benefit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136A(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the benefit and the person` `s 136A(1) council tax benefit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136A(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the benefit and the person` `s 136A(1) another income-related benefit` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 136A(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the benefit and the person` `s 136A(1) housing benefit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
